Operation Molot (Hammer)

Date: May 1981

Time Limit: 21 days

Situation:
The Khost Islamic Liberation Front holds the high ground across the province. Enemy forces operate from a fortified base complex in the south-east and have garrisoned villages along both the Khost-Gardez Pass and the Ghulam Khan Road. The garrison at Khost is resupplied by air and holds a pocket around the city and its two airfields. Everything beyond that pocket is contested.

Mission:
Break out of the Khost pocket and take the province.

Nine settlements are designated mission objectives: Gardez, Barak Kalay, Dey Khul, Caperi, Ayubkhel, Arghu, Pelon Kheyl, Khan Kala and Dabgay. They range from provincial road heads to hamlets of no economic weight whatever - the smallest of them still has to be taken.

Enemy Forces:
A fortified mountain base complex south-east of Khost, supported by artillery and anti-aircraft units. Garrison infantry holding the villages. Mobile raiding forces conducting ambush operations across the province.

Friendly Forces:
Soviet units deploy from the Khost pocket. Two airbases provide air support and resupply. Prestige drawn from the ground you hold may be spent on reinforcements as the operation proceeds - you will not finish this with the force you start with.

Victory Conditions:
Hold at least 5 of the 9 mission objectives when the operation ends. Fail that and the result is capped at a Draw no matter how much ground you have taken.

With the objectives in hand, your grade is set by the share of the province's value you control:

   38 percent - Minor Victory
   47 percent - Major Victory
   56 percent - Decisive Victory

You may end the operation early once a victory is in hand. Days you do not use pay a prestige bonus - weigh that against the better result another week of fighting might buy.
